Upstream attribution
================================================================================

KnegisWhisper is an independent application. It is not affiliated with,
endorsed by, or supported by either project below, and it depends on neither
project's hosted services, accounts, licensing, updaters, or telemetry.


OpenWhispr — source of ported code
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
    https://github.com/OpenWhispr/openwhispr
    Copyright (c) OpenWhispr contributors
    MIT License

Portions of KnegisWhisper are derived from OpenWhispr, which is MIT-licensed and
therefore compatible with this project's license. Copyright and license notices
in derived files are retained in those files.

Ported material is recorded per-integration in config/integration-manifest.json
and described in docs/PORTING_MATRIX.md. The baseline commit is recorded in
config/upstream-integration-baseline.json.


Pluely — design reference only, NO CODE COPIED
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
    https://github.com/iamsrikanthnani/pluely
    Copyright (c) Srikanth Nani
    GNU General Public License v3.0

Pluely is licensed under the GPL-3.0. KnegisWhisper is MIT-licensed, so no
Pluely source code is copied into this repository — copying it would make this
application a copyleft derivative.

Pluely was audited as a behavioural specification for Tauri window management,
non-activating overlay behaviour, and per-platform system-audio capture. Those
findings are documented in docs/UPSTREAM_AUDIT.md. The techniques described
there are implemented independently, and the third-party crates involved
(cpal, wasapi, cidre, libpulse-binding, hound, ringbuf, tauri-nspanel) are
obtained directly from their own authors under their own licenses.

Verbatim Pluely code in this repository would be a defect. Please report it.


================================================================================
Vendored fonts
================================================================================

Committed to this repository and served from the application bundle rather than
from a CDN. The production CSP is `font-src 'self'`, set in
apps/desktop/src-tauri/tauri.conf.json, so a hosted font would load during
`npm run dev` and fail silently in the packaged build.

    Geist             The Geist Project Authors (Vercel) — SIL OFL 1.1
                      apps/desktop/src/fonts/geist-variable.woff2
                      apps/desktop/src/fonts/OFL-Geist.txt

    Tiny5             The Tiny5 Project Authors — SIL OFL 1.1
                      apps/desktop/src/fonts/tiny5-400.woff2
                      apps/desktop/src/fonts/OFL-Tiny5.txt

    Doto              The Doto Project Authors — SIL OFL 1.1
                      apps/desktop/src/fonts/doto-round-variable.woff2
                      apps/desktop/src/fonts/OFL-Doto.txt

Taken from the Google Fonts repository (github.com/google/fonts, ofl/) and
modified only by subsetting to Latin and converting to WOFF2. Tiny5 is pinned
to its default instance and Doto to round dots (ROND 100); Geist and Doto keep
their weight axis. Each retains its license, which sits beside the file.


================================================================================
Bundled third-party components
================================================================================

The application downloads the following when the user installs them, from
Settings or the import screen, rather than vendoring them. Each is pinned by
version in config/sidecars.json and verified by digest; each retains its own
license.

    whisper.cpp                 MIT           ggml-org/whisper.cpp
    llama.cpp                   MIT           ggml-org/llama.cpp
    sherpa-onnx                 Apache-2.0    k2-fsa/sherpa-onnx
    ONNX Runtime                MIT           microsoft/onnxruntime
                                              (inside the sherpa-onnx archive)
    FFmpeg                      LGPL-2.1+     ffmpeg.org, via BtbN/FFmpeg-Builds
                                              (the lgpl variant)

config/sidecars.json also pins yt-dlp (Unlicense, yt-dlp/yt-dlp) for URL import,
which is withdrawn; no screen installs it.

The installer bundles one third-party file:

    Silero VAD v5.1.2 (ggml)    MIT           snakers4/silero-vad, converted by
                                              ggml-org/whisper-vad
                                              apps/desktop/src-tauri/resources/
                                              ggml-silero-v5.1.2.bin

Model weights are downloaded at the user's request and are covered by their own
licenses. config/provider-registry.json records each model's source repository.

The Rust crates and npm packages compiled into the application retain their own
licenses, recorded in Cargo.lock and apps/desktop/package-lock.json. No combined
third-party license list is generated or shipped with the installer yet
(KNEG-533).
